-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Stormbringer
  Publisher   Mastertronic Added Dimension, 1987
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Stormbringer (1987)(Mastertronic Added Dimension)[128K][Magic
              Knight 4].z80
  MD5         d462589b7b7e63cb7e958323d00d165a

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Magic Knight in silver-grey armour, painted as in
              Spellbound's Enhanced set (the same pictures); the characters
              and objects keep the game's own colours. A painted set,
              colourist not named.

  Changes     1.1: adds an Enhanced colour set: the Magic Knight in silver-
              grey armour, carried over from Spellbound's Enhanced set

  Note        Keys: Z and SPACE on the menu (PLAY GAME is the last line); N
              left, M right, A up, SPACE opens the command window. The Magic
              Knight, the characters and the objects are hardware sprites, so
              they keep their own colours instead of the scenery's; the rooms,
              the windows and the flying things in the castle stay as the game
              draws them.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite strength
   2  Infinite magic
   3  Infinite time

  From an archive .pok, each checked against this release's code: the stores
  after the strength, magic and time counts go down become loads. Not played.

