  Tested      NexClash differential verification against four recordings;
              simulated boot; run from its menu in OverSpec; Tang FPGA board:
              loads and plays.

  Replay      1.1 Enhanced (2026-11-21): IDENTICAL on the same four
              recordings, 62,450 frames, with 13,499 checks that no unpainted
              figure shows the changed palette entry; the default build is
              unchanged. 1.0: IDENTICAL on four machine-played recordings
              (62,450 frames: 63 rooms, command windows, the lightning that
              ends the game), negative controls detected

  Hardware    1.1 Enhanced (2026-11-21): Tang Nano 20K FPGA build of the Next,
              with DivMMC automap on and 124 sprites left visible by a
              previous program: loads, the Knight in grey armour, plays. 1.0:
              Tang Nano 20K FPGA build of the Next: loads with DivMMC automap
              on and plays

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
